{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["He said <b>the Mishkan, the Mishkan of the Testimony</b> — because the linen curtains (יריעות שש משזר) are called \"Mishkan\" both in the command (Exodus 26:1) and in the execution (Exodus 36:8), whereas \"the Mishkan of the Testimony\" encompasses the entire House as a whole, for it is the Mishkan made for the tablets of the Testimony.\n\nAccording to the opinion of the many (Rashi and Ibn Ezra), <b>\"These are the reckonings of the Mishkan\"</b> refers back to what was mentioned above — he would say that the Mishkan and its implements, namely the House and the courtyard and everything made for them, are the reckonings of the service of the Levites, which Moses reckoned by the hand of Ithamar, and that the holy vessels — the Ark, the Table, the Menorah, and the Altars — are not included in the Mishkan, for they were in the hand of Eleazar. But this is not my opinion, for why would he mention the reckoning of Ithamar and not mention the reckoning of Eleazar, which is the more weighty? Rather, \"These are the reckonings\" alludes to what he mentions further in the passage — he says that the silver of the reckoning of the congregation, one hundred talents, from which were made the sockets and the hooks of the pillars and their overlaying and their bands (Exodus 38:25–28), and the bronze of the waving, which is seventy talents, from which he made the bronze altar and its grating and all its utensils and the sockets of the courtyards and the pegs (Exodus 38:29–31) — all of it Moses gave by number, by weight, by the hand of Ithamar.\n\nHe did not recount in the passage what was made from the gold, for of the gold — part was in the hand of Ithamar: the overlaying of the planks and the bars; and part was in the hand of Eleazar: the Ark and the Cover, the Menorah, the Table, and the golden Altar. Now since it is not known how much gold-overlay each vessel contains, he did not state that Moses gave it to them by count and by weight. And for this reason he did not mention here the reckoning of Eleazar, for Scripture comes now to speak only of the making of the Mishkan, not of the journeys. And do not find it difficult that he counts here the bronze altar, which belongs to the reckoning of Eleazar — for he needed to say that they made it from the bronze of the waving, and he would not be particular to remove one item from the totality of the things about which he said that they are in the hand of Ithamar, for such is the way of Scripture in many places (Genesis 35:26; ibid. 46:27). Nor did he mention here the Basin and its stand, for it was not made by weight; rather, all the mirrors that the women who served at the entrance brought he placed into it, and Moses did not know its weight. And it is possible that it was not in the reckoning of Ithamar, for it may be included in what Scripture said (Numbers 3:31), \"and their charge shall be the Ark and the Table and the Menorah and the Altars and the holy vessels with which they minister\" — for with the Basin and its stand they minister at the altar, yet behold, it is not in the reckoning of this passage:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {0 "The parenthetical verse references inserted by the editor (e.g. Genesis 35:26; ibid. 46:27) are given here exactly as they appear in the source; the second reference is abbreviated in the Hebrew as 'שם' meaning 'there (ibid.).'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:23.787366996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}